# Why every setting, env var, header and command this gateway uses is here.
#
# The rule, from the published methodology: a setting may appear only if it is needed to boot the
# process at all, to point an upstream at the test mock instead of a real provider, to expose an
# ingress path the matrix exercises, or to bind the port and cores the rig requires. One claim per
# line: <pattern> <boot|upstream|ingress|bind>. Anything unclaimed is a lint failure, and a claim
# that matches nothing is a stale claim and also a failure.
#
# Migrated from GW_CONFIG_WHY in gateway.sh, which is dead code the lint was still reading.
# Claimed because the dead gateway.sh launcher still passes it and the lint reads that file. The
# LIVE config does not set it: the harness sets it for every gateway from the cores it pinned
# (manifest.rs's pinned_parallelism), so no entrant states its own.
GOMAXPROCS bind   # Go pre-1.25 reads the HOST cpu count, not the --cpuset-cpus limit
INITIAL_ROOT_TOKEN boot  # its relay routes serve nothing without a token it issued, and every token its admin API mints is server-chosen; this is the only way the declared auth is a real one
# This gateway has no config file. It keeps its configuration in a database and is configured
# through its own admin API after boot, so the deployment its operators run is these calls: log in,
# raise the quota so a throughput run cannot exhaust it, wire each upstream as a channel pointing at
# the mock, and create the API key the harness authenticates with. Every one of those is either
# booting the process into a usable state or pointing an upstream at the mock.
curl upstream  # the admin-API calls that wire this gateway's upstreams to the test mock

## Current channel configuration

The pinned v0.6.10 relay router implements OpenAI chat ingress. Four channels target the local mock by URL: OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini and Cohere v1; each must return nonempty assistant content during setup, and failure aborts measurement rather than producing a misleading result. A fifth, AWS (type 33, model claude-3-haiku-20240307), has no URL to point: relay/adaptor/aws builds a bedrockruntime client with only a region and static keys (from the channel config) and calls InvokeModel at the SDK's default https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com. Engine v1.2 resolves every name to the mock and makes the gateway trust the run's CA, so that cell is probed like any other; it is not gated at setup because its outcome is the cell's verdict.

Native Responses, Anthropic, Gemini, Cohere and Bedrock ingress are absent from router/relay.go and are excluded by the versioned capability matrix. Dashboard HTML is never inference evidence. Bedrock upstream uses the AWS SDK's InvokeModel at its default HTTPS host; with engine v1.2 it is measured through the catch-all DNS and the mock's TLS listener (upstream_transport "tls").

